Strings use double quotes. Supported escapes are backslash-n (new line), backslash-r (carriage return), backslash-t (tab), backslash-double-quote and two backslashes for one literal backslash.

A string literal cannot contain an actual line break; use an escape instead. String interpolation, character literals and string methods are not implemented.

